+## Failed session initialization
+
+- If `beforeSession` throws an `Error`, the orchestrator awaits `onError(session, error)` and then `afterSession(session)` before rejecting with the original error, provided those hooks succeed; user-input processing and model execution do not start. `afterSession` deliberately runs even after partial initialization: it cannot assume allocation completed or a model response exists, and deployers must track their own acquired resources so cleanup tolerates resources never allocated ([validated by: reports and cleans up a failed beforeSession before rejecting with the original error](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.acceptance.test.ts#L8)).
+
